{
  "raw": {
    "https://uwaterloo.ca/careers/": {
      "title": "Join Canada's innovation university",
      "description": "Join Canada's innovation university | Careers at Waterloo | University of Waterloo Skip to main content Jump to Jump to Admissions About Waterloo Faculties & Academics Offices & Services Support Waterloo Open Search Location Search for Search Location On all sites On this site Careers at Waterloo Menu Careers at Waterloo Home Current Opportunities Current Opportunities Current Waterloo Employees Future Waterloo Employees Faculty opportunities Affiliated and Federated institutions Executive opportunities Casual and other opportunities Hiring Process at Waterloo Commitment to Equity Human Resources Join Canada's innovation university At the University of Waterloo, you’ll have the opportunity to shape your future while contributing to meaningful change, where your career can thrive, and together, we can drive innovation, collaboration, and excellence. Join a world-class institution that empowers you to grow, innovate, and make an impact . As a valued team member, you'll receive a competitive salary, a defined-benefit pension plan, comprehensive extended health care, dental benefits, and group life insurance, including excellent vacation and leave policies, and more. SEE CURRENT JOB OPPORTUNITIES WHERE CAN WATERLOO TAKE YOU? HIRING PROCESS AT WATERLOO WHAT TO EXPECT At Waterloo, we believe that our greatest asset is our people. Let's build a bright future together. Work with the brightest Belong to a group of talented professionals who are working together to educate future leaders, conduct life-improving research , fuel a world-renowned start-up ecosystem and so much more. Expand your possibilities Benefit from lifelong learning opportunities , including tuition benefits for you and your children, workshops, leadership programs, mentoring, and events to enhance your skills and career. Make a difference together As a Waterloo employee, you will be a fundamental part of what makes our institution unique and unconventional. Together, we bring bold ideas and brilliant minds together to make a positive, global impact . Why Waterloo? WHO WE ARE We are a leading global research-intensive university, renowned for entrepreneurship and innovation, providing co-op and work-integrated learning at scale with impact. OUR MISSION We advance learning and knowledge through teaching, research, and scholarship, nationally and internationally, in an environment of free expression and enquiry . WHAT WE ENVISION A community of curious, collaborative, innovative and entrepreneurial problem-solvers and leaders who seek to understand and identify equitable and sustainable solutions for the future of humanity and our planet. Source: Waterloo at 100 Our Values We Think Differently We embrace bold, unconventional thinking, celebrate diversity, and challenge the status quo to drive innovation and shape the future. Learn more about Waterloo's Values. We Act With Purpose We are purpose-driven to make a positive impact, embrace responsibility, and value hands-on experiences to drive meaningful change. We Work Together We achieve our best work through collaboration, fostering a united community that drives positive change and innovation. DEFYING TRADITION “Waterloo was founded on a bold idea: that integrating academics with real-world experience could redefine higher education and strengthen society. That spirit of unconventional thinking remains its greatest strength, and I am excited to return to help build on that foundation.” DR. BILL ROSEHART University of Waterloo's Eighth President and Vice-Chancellor Employee health and well-being The University of Waterloo places a strong emphasis on employee health and well-being through a comprehensive and holistic approach to ensure a healthy workplace environment where all individuals are valued and can thrive. Key initiatives and programs, such as the Employee and Family Assistance Program (EFAP) , mental health resources and training, and wellness programs and events, foster a healthy and supportive work environment for all. Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion The University of Waterloo is committed to being a welcoming and inclusive community for all. The Office of Equity, Diversity, Inclusion and Anti-Racism (EDI-RO), working with faculty, staff and students, strive to lead efforts towards transformative culture change, disrupt oppressive systems, dismantle institutional barriers and embed anti-racism and equity in policies, processes, environments and experiences on campus. Learn more about our commitment to equity . Indigenous initiatives The University of Waterloo is deeply committed to Indigenization, decolonization, and reconciliation. Waterloo has launched a five-year Indigenous Strategic Plan aimed at building long-term relationships with Indigenous Peoples and communities based on respect and reciprocity. The University provides dedicated support and resources for Indigenous students, faculty, and staff. This includes the Office of Indigenous Relations , which plays a central role in advancing these initiatives. Join a University internationally recognized for global innovation and world-changing research Most innovative university in Canada for 30 of the last 33 years. Maclean's University Rankings 2025 3rd for highest quality among Canada's universities. Maclean's University Rankings 2025 97th in the world As ranked by more than 55,000 researchers and scholars from around the globe. Times Higher Education’s (THE) World Reputation Rankings for 2025 Where will Waterloo take you? Explore Waterloo Careers Information about Careers at Waterloo LinkedIn LinkedIn Human Resources East Campus 1 175 Columbia Street West Waterloo, ON, Canada N2L 3G1 519-888-4567, ext. 45935 Questions? Please contact us at hrhelp@uwaterloo.ca with any questions or comments. Workday access → Hiring manager support → Contact us → Information about the University of Waterloo University of Waterloo University of Waterloo 43.471468 -80.544205 Campus map Campus map 200 University Avenue West Waterloo , ON , Canada N2L 3G1 +1 519 888 4567 Contact Waterloo Campus status News Maps & directions Accessibility Careers Emergency notifications Privacy Feedback The University of Waterloo acknowledges that much of our work takes place on the traditional territory of the Neutral, Anishinaabeg, and Haudenosaunee peoples. Our main campus is situated on the Haldimand Tract, the land granted to the Six Nations that includes six miles on each side of the Grand River. Our active work toward reconciliation takes place across our campuses through research, learning, teaching, and community building, and is co-ordinated within the Office of Indigenous Relations . Instagram Instagram LinkedIn LinkedIn Facebook Facebook YouTube YouTube @uwaterloo social directory On It Check WHERE THERE’S A CHALLENGE, WATERLOO IS ON IT . Learn how   → ©2026 All rights reserved We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience Select 'Accept all' to agree and continue. You consent to our cookies if you continue to use this website. Accept all"
    },
    "https://uwaterloo.ca/careers/current-opportunities": {
      "title": "Current Opportunities",
      "description": "Current Opportunities | Careers at Waterloo | University of Waterloo Skip to main content Jump to Jump to Admissions About Waterloo Faculties & Academics Offices & Services Support Waterloo Open Search Location Search for Search Location On all sites On this site Careers at Waterloo Menu Careers at Waterloo Home Current Opportunities Current Opportunities Current Waterloo Employees Future Waterloo Employees Faculty opportunities Affiliated and Federated institutions Executive opportunities Casual and other opportunities Hiring Process at Waterloo Commitment to Equity Human Resources Current Opportunities At the University of Waterloo, we create and promote a culture where everyone can reach their full potential. As an employee, you get support & opportunities that empower you to advance your career. Explore how You + Waterloo can bring big ideas to life, together. The University is a welcoming workplace for those of all abilities, interests, and expertise. As part of our workforce, you can do what you do best, every day. Reinvent your career. Reimagine your future. Explore our current opportunities. All staff employees , regardless of internal status , will apply through the internal portal housed within the Jobs Hub on Workday or through the Current Waterloo Employee Opportunities section of the Careers website. Check out the Job Hub Demo for Current Waterloo Employees . Current Waterloo Employees Future Waterloo Employees Executive Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Affiliated and Federated Institutions of Waterloo (AFIW) Casual and other opportunities Secondments and temporary reassignments: Secondments are fixed-term opportunities for a regular staff member to gain valuable experience in another organizational unit with the knowledge that the staff member will return to their existing position when the term of the secondment has ended. An agreement between the University, the staff member, as well as the two organizational unit heads, the hiring manager and current staff manager, and Human Resources is required. A secondment typically occurs between departments, and the position is advertised campus-wide. View secondment opportunities . Temporary Reassignments are similar to secondments in that they are temporary opportunities. The difference is that these roles are within the employee’s home department, and as such, if the position is advertised, the advertising for the opportunity is internal to the department. Career Support for University Employees Discover valuable Career Development resources available to Waterloo staff and book an appointment with Sarah Lewis, your Employee Career Advisor and Learning Specialist. EMPLOYEE LOG IN REQUIRED CAREER DEVELOPMENT RESOURCES Information about Careers at Waterloo LinkedIn LinkedIn Human Resources East Campus 1 175 Columbia Street West Waterloo, ON, Canada N2L 3G1 519-888-4567, ext. 45935 Questions? Please contact us at hrhelp@uwaterloo.ca with any questions or comments. Workday access → Hiring manager support → Contact us → Information about the University of Waterloo University of Waterloo University of Waterloo 43.471468 -80.544205 Campus map Campus map 200 University Avenue West Waterloo , ON , Canada N2L 3G1 +1 519 888 4567 Contact Waterloo Campus status News Maps & directions Accessibility Careers Emergency notifications Privacy Feedback The University of Waterloo acknowledges that much of our work takes place on the traditional territory of the Neutral, Anishinaabeg, and Haudenosaunee peoples. Our main campus is situated on the Haldimand Tract, the land granted to the Six Nations that includes six miles on each side of the Grand River. Our active work toward reconciliation takes place across our campuses through research, learning, teaching, and community building, and is co-ordinated within the Office of Indigenous Relations . Instagram Instagram LinkedIn LinkedIn Facebook Facebook YouTube YouTube @uwaterloo social directory On It Check WHERE THERE’S A CHALLENGE, WATERLOO IS ON IT . Learn how   → ©2026 All rights reserved We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience Select 'Accept all' to agree and continue. You consent to our cookies if you continue to use this website. Accept all"
    },
